#N canvas 100 100 700 540 10;
#X obj 40 40 jet_win;
#X msg 40 80 create;
#X msg 130 80 destroy;
#X obj 40 130 jet_head 0;
#X obj 40 165 jet_color 0.3 0.7 1;
#X obj 40 200 jet_square 2;
#X floatatom 40 250 5 0 8 0 - - -;
#X text 40 275 half size;
#X msg 140 250 size 1;
#X msg 220 250 size 3;
#X text 40 320 [jet_square] is a square like Gem's [square]. The size is the HALF side length \, exactly as in Gem and in jet_rectangle\: [jet_square 2] is 4 units wide and 4 tall. With the default camera the window is 8 units tall \, so [jet_square 4] is as tall as the picture. It is centred on the origin of the chain - move it with jet_translateXYZ \, turn it with jet_rotateXYZ \, colour it with jet_color. If a texture is current (jet_perlin \, jet_video \, an effect ...) the square shows it \, tinted by the chain colour.;
#X text 40 440 Inlets\: the chain (bang \, plus "size s") and the half size. The size inlet only stores - the shape is drawn on the next bang from the chain. The bang is forwarded out of the outlet.;
#X connect 1 0 0 0;
#X connect 2 0 0 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 6 0 5 1;
#X connect 8 0 5 0;
#X connect 9 0 5 0;
